{
  "configuration_id": "config_010",
  "reason": "With only one completed experiment (config_001: rna_only/singleprofile/pca_n2000 at ~48.5% accuracy), evidence is extremely sparse. The most critical uncertainty is whether the image modality carries discriminative signal at all, which determines the entire direction of the search (RNA-focused vs. image-focused vs. multimodal). config_010 (image_only, singleprofile, resnet50) is the cleanest single-variable comparison to config_001: it changes only the modality while keeping the profile setting (singleprofile) and architecture simplicity (no aggregation, no fusion) identical. If image-only substantially outperforms RNA-only, we should prioritize image encoders and multimodal fusion; if it underperforms, RNA is the dominant signal and we should focus on RNA encoder and profile choices. This experiment maximally reduces uncertainty about the most consequential design axis before committing budget to more complex multimodal or multiprofile configurations."
}

